.TH SUPERJUICE 1 "November 2026" "polajuice @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
superjuice \- motion front-end of the polajuice engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B superjuice
.I INPUT.mp4
.B \-c
.I CAMERA
.RB [ \-o
.IR OUTPUT.mp4 ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ffmpeg ... \-f yuv4mpegpipe \- |
.B superjuice \-c
.I CAMERA
.B | ffmpeg ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B superjuice
runs every frame of a movie through the same look pipeline as
.BR polajuice (1):
camera, film, development, aging. Grain is decorrelated frame to frame
("boiling"), and cameras with motion character (super8, autochrome,
technicolor-3strip) add gate weave and flicker.
.PP
In
.B file mode
one command does the decoding, rendering, encoding and audio
passthrough; it needs
.BR ffmpeg (1)
on the PATH. The default output is
.IR INPUT_CAMERA.mp4
next to the input.
.PP
In
.B plumbing mode
.B superjuice
reads YUV4MPEG on standard input and writes it on standard output, for
custom pipelines:
.PP
.nf
    ffmpeg \-i clip.mov \-f yuv4mpegpipe \-pix_fmt yuv420p \- \\
      | superjuice \-c super8 \\
      | ffmpeg \-f yuv4mpegpipe \-i \- \-c:v libx264 \-crf 18 out.mp4
.fi
.PP
Instant cameras are still-print formats and are refused.
.SH OPTIONS
The look options are those of
.BR polajuice (1)
and mean the same:
.BR \-c / \-\-camera ,
.BR \-f / \-\-film ,
.BR \-\-no\-film ", " \-\-any\-film ", " \-\-develop ", " \-\-crop ", "
.BR \-\-temp ", " \-\-tint ", " \-\-black ", " \-\-shadows ", " \-\-highlights ", "
.BR \-\-contrast ", " \-\-grad ", " \-\-gradangle ", " \-\-gradpos ", "
.BR \-\-denoise ", " \-\-distortion ", " \-\-devignette ", " \-\-rotate ", "
.BR \-\-trimx ", " \-\-trimy ", " \-\-trimw ", " \-\-trimh ", "
.BR \-\-age ", " \-\-strength ", " \-\-grain ", " \-\-edge ", " \-\-ev ", "
.BR \-\-halation ", " \-\-filter ", " \-\-recipe .
.PP
Movie-specific:
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " INTEGER"
Base seed; each frame's grain is derived from it.
.TP
.BI \-\-motion\-scale " N"
Scale gate weave and flicker (default 1; 0.5 steadier, 2 a worn
projector, 0 tripod-locked).
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " PATH"
Output movie (file mode).
.TP
.BI \-\-crf " N"
H.264 quality for file mode, lower is better (default 18).
.SH FILES
The film library and print stocks are found as for
.BR polajuice (1):
.BR $POLAJUICE_FILMS ,
.BR $POLAJUICE_HOME ,
the source tree,
.IR ~/.local/share/polajuice ,
the build's datadir.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR polajuice (1),
.BR super8ify (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1).
